title: First live run against real providers, and a change of visual direction
---
date: 2026-10-17
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: Live testing with Strata and LM Studio exposed two adapter bugs, and the owner rejected the generic interface in favor of a close GobboNet match.
---
tags: ai, interface, prototype
---
source_commit: c5b43a64be55f81e91d492d0c06f2df22d21a6a7
---
body:

Step seven ran the application against real servers, and the live run found
defects that the fake provider could not.

LM Studio rejected requests with an unsupported media type error because the
outbound client had not set a JSON content type. The same run showed that its
stream carries no timing statistics, so the adapter now measures time to first
token and estimates throughput itself, while still preferring provider-supplied
timings when they exist. Both bugs were reproduced as failing tests before they
were fixed.

The same run exercised the behaviors the design promised. One conversation kept
its history and distinct provenance when switched from one model to another,
concurrent conversations on one server were serialized, Stop saved partial
replies as cancelled, and Ctrl+C during a stream saved the partial text, released
the lock, and left the database intact.

Two items were not finished. Provider authentication and the cold-start checks
were deferred by the owner, not waived. And the owner rejected the shell's
appearance, asking for a pixel-for-pixel match to GobboNet except where
Labbonet's model dynamics require a difference. That requirement redirected the
work toward the parity effort described in the next entries.

[Commit c5b43a6](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/c5b43a64be55f81e91d492d0c06f2df22d21a6a7)
